        "original_id": "0282605f-bfea-545d-9547-6e0c3c3c97dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Gasquet, Tatiana Golovin, Jim Pugh, Nick Kyrgios\n- Events: 2004 French Open, 2015 Estoril Open – Singles\n- Roles: professional tennis player, doubles specialist\n\nFacts:\n- Jim Pugh was born on February 5, 1964, in Burbank, California, and he is a former professional tennis player from the United States.\n- Jim Pugh was a doubles specialist who won three Grand Slam men's doubles titles, including two Australian Open titles and one Wimbledon title.\n- Jim Pugh won five Grand Slam mixed doubles titles, including three Australian Open titles, one Wimbledon title, and one US Open title.\n- Richard Gasquet won the mixed doubles Grand Slam title at the 2004 French Open with partner Tatiana Golovin.\n- Richard Gasquet won the 2015 Estoril Open singles title by defeating Nick Kyrgios in the final 6–3, 6–2.",
